The following example selects all elements with a class attribute value that 
contains "te":

The CSS attribute selectors can be useful for styling form elements, based on 
input type:

Tip:Visit ourCSS Forms Tutorialfor more examples on how to style forms with CSS.

### Code Examples

```
[class^="top"] {
background: yellow;
}

---

[class$="test"] {
background: yellow;
}

---

[class*="te"] {
background: yellow;
}

---

input[type="text"] {
width: 150px;
padding: 6px;
margin-bottom: 10px;
background-color: pink;
}
input[type="button"] {
width: 100px;
padding: 6px;
background-color: lightgreen;
}
```

